## 6. Running the whole suite

### Per-mode round-trips (one ELF at a time)

```sh
./andes-sim run tests/fixtures/rt_c_v_matmul.elf      --mode hybrid --trigger marker --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium
./andes-sim run tests/fixtures/rt_c_v_matmul_free.elf --mode hybrid --trigger pc --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium \
  --pc-start vmatmul_kernel --pc-end 0x<post-jal>
./andes-sim run tests/fixtures/rt_c_v_matmul_free.elf --mode hybrid --trigger icount --engine vsim:ax45mpv_premium
./hsim.py run tests/fixtures/rt_c_v_matmul_free.elf --mode simpoint \
  --interval 100 --max-k 2
```

Each prints a headline figure: `./andes-sim run --mode hybrid` prints `[marker window_cycles] N`, `[pc window_cycles] N`, or `[icount window_cycles] N`; `./hsim.py run --mode simpoint` prints `estimated_cycles=N`.

### Parallel runner (scripts/run_e2e.sh)

```sh
JOBS=8 bash scripts/run_e2e.sh
```

Runs every e2e fixture in parallel under a FIFO job pool.

> The e2e suite is driven from the parent repo by `scripts/run_e2e.sh`, not
> by CTest. The vsim submodule keeps only the hybrid-layer doctest unit
> tests; there is no CTest `switching-mode` label.

> CAUTION: on this 128-core host the default `JOBS` value can saturate the
> box and time out. Use `JOBS=8` as a practical cap.

